{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>For she saw, etc. And she, etc.</b> One needs to know why it was necessary to say <b>and she</b>, and it would have sufficed to say ״she was not given,״ etc. — for it is obvious that he is speaking of her. Perhaps it is because the verse stated two things: the first — that she saw that Shelah had grown, and it is obvious that the statement of her father-in-law who said ״until he grows,״ etc. was not fulfilled, for she was still in her father's house; and the second — <b>and she was not given</b>, etc., meaning that she saw through ruach ha-kodesh that it was not fitting for her to be given to him as a wife, and therefore she arose and acted and succeeded. Go forth and learn what came forth from her to the world — from women in the tent shall she be blessed."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:46:51.673053786Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}